Id: apa001w
Severity: WARN, INFO
Category: services
Check: check_apache
Fix: Give each Listen directive an address (Listen 192.0.2.10:80) and restart.
References: Apache httpd core directives (Listen)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, CM-7; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

The Apache server is listening on every address of the machine instead
of one named address (a Listen directive without an IP, or with
0.0.0.0 or [::], or no Listen directive at all); every such Listen
is named in the one finding. On a machine with more than one
interface this serves the site where it was never meant to be
served. The same id at
INFO level confirms the server does listen only on one address and
port. Give each Listen directive an explicit address, for example
"Listen 192.0.2.10:80", and restart the server.
